<testsuite name="owlwarden:fixtures/vulnerable/next-api" tests="21" failures="21" errors="0" skipped="0" time="0.120">
  <testcase classname="sql-injection" name="app/api/login/route.ts:16:5" time="0">
    <failure type="sql-injection" message="[high] SQL query built by string interpolation (likely)">A value taken from the request is interpolated into SQL, so the caller controls part of the statement. That is enough to read other users&apos; rows, bypass a WHERE clause, or drop a table.
OWASP: A03:2021
CWE-89
Fix: Use a parameterised query, or Prisma&apos;s tagged $queryRaw which binds automatically.</failure>
  </testcase>
  <testcase classname="ssrf" name="app/api/proxy/route.ts:19:28" time="0">
    <failure type="ssrf" message="[high] Server fetches a URL the caller controls (likely)">The destination of this request comes from the caller, so they choose which host the server connects to. That includes hosts they cannot reach themselves: the cloud metadata endpoint that hands out IAM credentials, internal services that skip authentication because they are &apos;not exposed&apos;, and anything bound to localhost.
OWASP: A10:2021
CWE-918
Fix: Validate the URL in the route handler before fetching, and disable redirect following.</failure>
  </testcase>
