    <failure type="ssrf" message="[high] Server fetches a URL the caller controls (likely)">The destination of this request comes from the caller, so they choose which host the server connects to. That includes hosts they cannot reach themselves: the cloud metadata endpoint that hands out IAM credentials, internal services that skip authentication because they are &apos;not exposed&apos;, and anything bound to localhost.
